1
00:00:01,048 --> 00:00:06,319
ReproDesk: capture a bug once, give developers the evidence.

2
00:00:06,399 --> 00:00:11,872
Demo app: Northwind Gear, a web shop with two deliberate bugs.

3
00:00:12,715 --> 00:00:20,635
One click on the toolbar icon arms ReproDesk for this tab only. Chrome
requires that explicit action, so nothing records silently.

4
00:00:20,715 --> 00:00:28,635
Armed: a rolling buffer keeps only the last 90 seconds, locally. No keystrokes
are collected and only this tab is recorded.

5
00:00:28,715 --> 00:00:41,661
Test as usual: ReproDesk quietly keeps the latest moments in its buffer.

6
00:00:41,741 --> 00:00:49,663
Something looked wrong? Save last replay (Alt+Shift+R) keeps what just
happened, so there is no need to reproduce it.

7
00:00:49,743 --> 00:00:57,661
For a known bug, start a Repro Session: the whole path is recorded, plus 30
seconds of context from before the start.

8
00:00:57,741 --> 00:01:04,200
Bug 1: the promo code SUMMER20 shows a discount, but the total does not
change.

9
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:10,322
Add a marker to flag the moment. A screenshot is taken automatically.

10
00:01:10,402 --> 00:01:25,173
Fill in the checkout form. Typed text is never stored as events; the pixels
can be hidden later, before sharing.

11
00:01:25,253 --> 00:01:34,363
Bug 2: Place order fails with error E-4021.

12
00:01:34,443 --> 00:01:41,651
Look at another tab and recording pauses by itself. Nothing from other tabs is
ever stored.

13
00:01:41,731 --> 00:01:45,883
Back on the approved tab, capture resumes.

14
00:01:45,963 --> 00:01:52,000
Finish & review stops the recording and opens the report.

15
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:59,475
Review: the video, a live timeline and steps drafted from what really
happened. No AI guesses.

16
00:01:59,555 --> 00:02:05,283
Click any row of the timeline to jump to that moment in the video.

17
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:19,232
Hide sensitive data before sharing: open a screenshot, blur the card number
and box the error.

18
00:02:19,312 --> 00:02:26,101
The original screenshot is never modified. Only the exported copy carries the
blur.

19
00:02:26,979 --> 00:02:50,914
Do the same for video: mask the card field. The preview shows exactly what
will be exported.

20
00:02:51,792 --> 00:02:59,085
Describe what happened and what you expected. The expected result is always
written by you.

21
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:08,610
One click exports an Evidence Package, an HTML report and a Word report.

22
00:03:08,690 --> 00:03:17,199
The HTML report is self-contained, with the blurred screenshots, so developers
can open it anywhere.

23
00:03:17,279 --> 00:03:25,202
Everything stays on this device until you export it. Administrators can lock
settings and restrict sites with standard browser policies.

24
00:03:25,282 --> 00:03:28,782
ReproDesk: evidence instead of retelling.
